Wallbrook (part of Anthesis Group) is seeking experienced researchers to join our top-ranked global Business Intelligence team. Successful candidates will have proven experience working in a fast-paced research environment, excellent qualitative analytical skills, and a track record of producing high quality research for use in a commercial setting. 

Candidates should have a strong knowledge of international and regional business and political environments – and have business proficiency in at least one European language – as well as an innate sense of curiosity about international affairs, business and global markets more generally. 

We are looking for specialists to be based out of our office in London.

The exact responsibilities will vary depending on the role offered. However, we broadly look for the below skills when considering applicants for all our positions: 

• Manage complex open source and human intelligence-led investigative assignments (including pre-transactional integrity due diligence checks and other bespoke investigations); 
• Write concise and cogent reports that weave in research findings with an in-depth contextualized analysis of key issues and other pertinent findings; 
• Deliver written and verbal briefings to senior management and clients on research findings; 
• Prepare proposals for new business; 
• Support the development of our human source network in regions of expertise; and 
• Once comfortable with our house style and research methodologies, assist in training new team members and proof reading reports.

Essential Requirements: 

• Fluency reading and writing English in a commercial context and business proficiency in at least one European language. Other languages are a bonus; 
• 1-4 years’ full-time post-graduate work experience in the corporate intelligence industry and/or another relevant investigative background; 
• Outstanding communication and interpersonal skills.
• Experience using open source research tools such as LexisNexis and Factiva, as well as regional and language-specific databases and media sources; 
• Ability to plan and manage multifaceted research projects from the proposal stage to delivering our work to the client; 
• A working knowledge of financial, commercial and legal concepts; 
• A bachelor’s degree in a relevant field from an accredited university; 
• Professional proficiency using Microsoft Office Suite. Candidates should also have demonstrable skills in the following areas: 
• A keen interest in international affairs and business, including in Western Europe, and other regions of expertise;
• Ability to work both independently and as part of a team; 
• A proactive, can-do mindset and willingness to work outside job specifications when required; 
• An ability to thrive under pressure and work to tight deadlines; 
• Maintain a high level of professionalism in all areas of work; 
• Respond well to development feedback.

💎Full Time / Worldwide

✅Job responsibilities:  
1. Responsible for mobile client software architecture design and basic component development; 
2. Responsible for formulating key technical routes and technological evolution; 
3. Responsible for performance and experience optimization; 
4. Responsible for regularly evaluating work quality and progress during the development process to ensure a controllable development cycle; 
5. Responsible for work arrangements, progress control, and team building within the Android development group. 

✅Job requirements: 
1. Bachelor degree or higher, major in computer science and software engineering, more than 5 years of work experience, and at least 5 years of Android development experience; 
2. Proficient at Android development, with abundant development experience, proficient at complex business development; 
3. Deep understanding of underlying app principles, proficient in runtime, runloop, database, multi-threading, network, push and other development processes; 
4. Experience in basic component development and architecture, able to quickly design, build, debug, or refactor large-scale software code; 
5. Proficient in Android UI interface, animation drawing, multi-threading, and with a deep understanding of and experience with network communication protocols such as HTTP/HTTPS/Socket; 
6. In-depth and systematic understanding of performance optimization, and abundant practical experience; 
7. Multi-terminal cross-platform development experience; 
8. Inquiring spirit, good ability to learn, and strong enterprising and innovative consciousness; 
9. Strong sense of responsibility, team spirit, and good at writing technical documents. 
Prefered: 
- Android reverse development and security protection experience; 
- A long-term accumulation of technology blogs, Github has released the source code.

