Do you want to develop your career and make an impact in the fast-growth, fast-moving B2B technology space?

At Informa TechTarget, you’ll collaborate and grow alongside some of the industry’s most respected experts. You’ll work with leading brands and be exposed to world-shaping innovations. You’ll apply your energy and intellect to helping clients be faster to market and faster to revenue.

We’re a vibrant community of world-class practitioners – over 2000 colleagues strong – with offices in 19 locations around the world. We’re traded on Nasdaq and also part of Informa PLC, a global leader in business-to-business events, digital services, and academic research in the FTSE 100.

About Informa TechTarget

Informa TechTarget (Nasdaq: TTGT) informs, influences and connects the world’s technology buyers and sellers, to accelerate growth from R&D to ROI.

With an unparalleled reach of over 220 highly targeted technology-specific websites and more than 50 million permissioned first-party audience members, Informa TechTarget has a unique understanding of and insight into technology markets.

Underpinned by those audiences and their data, we offer expert-led, data-driven, and digitally enabled services that deliver significant impact and measurable outcomes to our clients. We provide our customers with:

- Trusted information that shapes the industry and informs investment
- Intelligence and advice that guides and influences strategy
- Advertising that grows reputation and establishes thought leadership
- Custom content that engages and prompts action
- Intent and demand generation that more precisely targets and converts

Our organization is committed to sustainability, diversity, wellbeing, and ethical working practices. Visit informatechtarget.com and follow us on LinkedIn.

The Campaign Manager is primarily responsible for supporting the management of delivery of products on a contract from inception to completion to ensure complete customer satisfaction. This includes the day-to-day responsibility of coordinating the reconfirming of what the customer purchased, capturing customer soft goals to communicate to all post sales teams, collection/receipt of online media deliverables, handling all post sale changes. Candidates must be logical thinkers with good communication skills who are able to multi-task and work under pressure. This individual needs to be a team player, detail-oriented and comfortable working in a fast-paced environment.

Essential Job Functions:

- Coordinate the receipt of online creative materials from Agencies and/or Advertisers to ensure creative deadlines are met for all media campaigns;
- Build relationship with Advertisers to provide support and to fulfill campaign in order to help build a loyal customer base;
- Communicate with the Sales, Customer Success, Product Operations teams about campaign status, performance and execution;
- Provide excellent Customer Service by responding to internal and external customer inquiries over the telephone and through email;
- Provide order status and performance updates to Sales Reps;
- Ensure proper revenue forecasting and recognition on a weekly basis;
- Setting up auto-reporting and ownership of any manual client reporting deliveries;
- Processing Campaign Changes including working with sales and clients to set proper expectations around impact and timing;
- Securing any necessary proof of delivery and processing month end close tasks

Qualifications

- Experience working as a Customer Service Representative or Sales Administrator is a plus, but not a must;
- Excellent oral and written communication skills;
- Strong organizational skills;
- Extremely reliable - team player;
- Professional phone skills;
- Must have the ability to handle multiple deadlines, phone calls and projects;
- Must be fast thinker and be able to make decisions quickly;
- Computer Application literate;
- B.A. or B.S. degree required;
- Proven sales and client management abilities, preferably to the advertising and agency marketplace; and,
- Accurate data entry skills, problem solving ability and the ability to work independently.

Additional Information

TechTarget, Inc., doing business as Informa TechTarget, including its subsidiaries is an equal opportunity employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local fair employment practices laws. We strictly prohibit and do not tolerate discrimination against employees, applicants, or any other covered persons because of race, color, sex (including pregnancy), age, national origin or ancestry, ethnicity, religion, creed, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, status as a veteran, and basis of disability or any other federal, state or local protected class. This policy applies to all terms and conditions of employment, including, but not limited to, hiring, training, promotion, discipline, compensation, benefits, and termination of employment. If you would like to request reasonable adjustments or accommodations to assist your participation in the hiring process and, or in the advertised position, please inform the appropriate Talent Acquisition Partner for the role once they have been in touch. Your request will be reviewed and considered in confidence.

Informa TechTarget complies with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), as amended by the ADA Amendments Act, and all applicable federal, state or local law.

We believe that great things happen when people connect face-to-face. That's why we work in-person with each other, or with customers and partners, three days a week or more. When you’re not spending time together in one of our offices or other workplaces – like at an Informa event – you get the flexibility and support to work from home or remotely.

Our benefits include:

- Great community: a welcoming culture with in-person and online social events, our fantastic Walk the World charity day and active colleague groups and networks promoting a positive, supportive, and collaborative work environment
- Broader impact: take up to four days per year to volunteer with a philanthropic organization
- Career opportunity: the opportunity to develop your career with bespoke training and learning, mentoring platforms and on-demand access to thousands of courses on LinkedIn Learning. When it’s time for the next step, we encourage and support internal job moves 
- Time out: Open Vacation, plus 10 national holidays, and the chance to work from (almost!) anywhere for up to four weeks a year 
- Competitive benefits, including a 401k match, health, vision and dental insurance, parental leave and an ESPP offering company shares at a minimum 15% discount 
- Strong wellbeing support through EAP assistance, mental health first aiders, free access to a wellness app and more 
- Recognition for great work, with global awards and kudos programs 
- As an international company, the chance to collaborate with teams around the world

Claims Handler (LLP)
Department: Professional and Commercial Risk - Claims Handling
Employment Type: Permanent
Location: Bristol 

Description
Our Professional Negligence Team specialises in advising professionals and their insurers when negligence claims arise. We work across a variety of service lines, including law, construction, architecture, property consultants, financial services, and accounting, offering tailored advice for each sector. Our expertise covers a wide range of claims, from straightforward disputes to complex, high-value cases, assessing professional standards and mitigating risks for our clients. We also handle Management Liability claims i.e. directors and officers and employment practices liability claims. 

We take a proactive approach to resolving disputes, often employing creative solutions to avoid litigation where possible. The team is also well-versed in alternative dispute resolution methods, such as mediation, helping to achieve favourable outcomes efficiently and cost-effectively. Through our deep knowledge of industry-specific standards and regulations, we ensure that our clients receive expert guidance on navigating claims in their respective fields.

The Professional Negligence Team sits within the wider Professional and Commercial Risks team in our Bristol office. The team is ranked in Tier 1 in both the Legal 500 and Chambers directories, with a number of leading individuals named. It includes commercial litigation together with the longest established professional negligence team in Bristol, acting for most of the leading insurers, as well as large professional services firms themselves including leading global surveyors, solicitors and insurance brokers. Alongside the team sits a market leading claims handling team, DAC Beachcroft Specialist Claims Services, handling several thousand professional indemnity claims on an outsourced basis on behalf of London Market Insurers. 

This role is a claims handling/paralegal role within the Professional Negligence Team handling Professional Negligence claims, Directors and Officers and Employment Practices Liability claims.

Key Responsibilities
The overall purpose of this role is to provide a timely, professional and high-quality service to clients in the management of Professional Negligence and Management Liability claims. The role will require you to: 

• Manage a caseload of lower value claims under supervision. This will include developing a knowledge of professional indemnity law, employment practices liability, insurance law and coverage issues as well as the civil procedure rules and aspects of alternative dispute resolution. The role will provide training and supervision with a view to enabling you to independently assess liability and quantum, and advise on strategy for a claim; 

• Conduct the review of new cases;

• Drafting correspondence to clients; 

• Maintain ongoing contact with the insurer and insured professional throughout the process to report on progress and take further instructions; 

• Instruct experts and external counsel where appropriate; 

• Complete administrative tasks; 

• Handle confidential information in line with the firms data security protocols. 

Skills, Knowledge and Expertise

• Graduate calibre with an excellent academic record; 

• Previous experience of working as a claims handler or similar within the field of professional indemnity is useful but not essential; 

• IT literate with working knowledge of Word and Excel. 

• Able to work to deadlines, prioritise own workload effectively under pressure and manage conflicting priorities; 

• Proactive and demonstrating initiative in driving forward matters on own accord, seeking guidance and input from others where appropriate; 

• Very good attention to detail and accuracy with drafting; 

• Team oriented. A collegiate approach to sharing knowledge and working with colleagues across locations is essential; 

• Committed and enthusiastic with a mature attitude to work and a desire to commit long term to a career in this field; 

• Confident oral and written communication skills.

Additional Information
As a Disability Confident Scheme employer, we’re committed to providing an inclusive and accessible recruitment process. If you need any reasonable adjustments at any stage (including the application, assessment or interview process), please contact recruitment@dacbeachcroft.com in confidence with the vacancy reference in the subject line, and we’ll be happy to help.

When you join Exclaimer you will join a global award-winning SaaS provider with an exceptional revenue rate, ambitious growth plans, and an inclusive and outcomes-driven culture.

Exclaimer is a high-growth SaaS company with 300+ colleagues across the UK, US, Europe, and Asia-Pacific. We promote a people-first culture built on fairness, inclusion, psychological safety, and continuous learning. As we evolve into a multi-channel platform for branded business communications, we offer employees the opportunity to shape the future of global communication—while growing their careers in a culture where curiosity, creativity, and accountability thrive. &nbsp;

We’re officially Great Place To Work Certified™

Exclaimer has been recognised by Great Place To Work® for our culture of collaboration, trust, and growth. This certification reflects our commitment to creating an environment where every voice matters and people genuinely enjoy coming to work.&nbsp; See our accreditations to learn more: Great Place to Work® UK | Great Place To Work® USA

&nbsp;

About the opportunity 👇

About the Role&nbsp;

You will be the in-house design lead for Exclaimer's marketing team, setting the standard for how our brand looks and feels wherever customers and prospects meet it. This is a hands-on role covering campaign creative, paid ads, web and landing page design, events, and motion, working closely with the brand, content, demand generation, and product marketing teams.&nbsp;

You'll also own quality. Our creative now comes from several places: in-house templates, AI-assisted production, freelancers, and agencies. You'll decide what you design yourself, what can be built from templates or with AI tools, and what goes to an agency, then review the output so everything we publish is consistent and on-brand.&nbsp;

Speed matters too. Our core web pages need redesigning for answer engine optimization (AEO), and our partner and account-based marketing (ABM) programs are growing. You will help us move faster by building reusable, easy-to-use design systems and by using AI design tools with a designer's eye for quality.&nbsp;

Key Responsibilities&nbsp;

Brand Consistency &amp; Quality Control&nbsp;

• Own the Exclaimer visual identity, keeping the brand system, templates, and guidelines current and easy to use&nbsp;

• Review creative from across the team, freelancers, agencies, and AI tools, and give clear, constructive feedback so everything we publish meets brand standards&nbsp;

• Together with the Brand team, decide which requests you design yourself and which are delegated to agencies or produced from templates or with AI, based on audience, visibility, and shelf life&nbsp;

• Build reusable, well-documented templates in Figma and/or Canva that colleagues can edit by hand or use with AI tools such as Claude&nbsp;

• Brief, direct, and review work from external design partners, and make handovers simple&nbsp;

Campaign &amp; Paid Creative&nbsp;

• Design full campaign asset sets so every touchpoint is consistent, including social ads, web banners, display ads, email and email signature banners, landing page graphics, and infographics&nbsp;

• Create conversion-focused ads for LinkedIn and other paid channels, working to each platform's specs and producing variations for testing&nbsp;

• Turn product imagery and UI into polished digital assets for paid, web, and sales enablement&nbsp;

• Tailor assets for partner and ABM programs, understanding the nuances between audiences&nbsp;

• Work with demand generation to use performance data to improve ad creative&nbsp;

Web &amp; Landing Pages&nbsp;

• Design page layouts, outlines, and imagery for landing pages and core website pages, applying UX best practice&nbsp;

• Work with the web, content, and SEO teams to speed up the redesign of core pages for AEO&nbsp;

• Hand off Figma designs clearly to developers and web agencies&nbsp;

Events &amp; Creative Concepts&nbsp;

• Bring creative ideas to events, activations, and content assets, from concept through to production files&nbsp;

• Design event materials across formats, from large-format banners and lightbox graphics to digital signage loops and giveaways&nbsp;

• Prepare print-ready artwork and work with print suppliers&nbsp;

AI-Enabled Design&nbsp;

• Use AI design tools (for example Midjourney, Adobe Firefly, Runway, and Claude) to speed up production&nbsp;

• Test new tools and workflows, and document guidelines so the wider team can use them well&nbsp;

• Review every AI output for accuracy, brand voice, and quality before it ships&nbsp;

Delivery &amp; Collaboration&nbsp;

• Manage several campaigns and requests at once, prioritize clearly, and keep stakeholders informed of timelines&nbsp;

• Work with brand, content, demand generation, product marketing, web, and channel teams to understand what each asset needs to achieve&nbsp;

Requirements&nbsp;

• Five or more years of experience in brand, marketing, or graphic design, ideally in a B2B, SaaS, or tech environment&nbsp;

• A portfolio showing consistent brand execution across web, ads, social, and sales content&nbsp;

• Expert Figma skills, including components, variants, Auto Layout, and variables. Experience limited to Canva is not enough for this role&nbsp;

• Experience maintaining a brand system, templates, and guidelines for others to use&nbsp;

• Proven experience designing conversion-focused ads, with knowledge of specs and best practice across LinkedIn, Meta, and display&nbsp;

• UX knowledge for landing page and website layouts&nbsp;

• Confident, active use of AI design tools (for example Midjourney, Firefly, Runway, and Claude), and a view on what the latest and best options are&nbsp;

• Ability to use AI critically, knowing when and how to apply it while maintaining brand quality and accuracy&nbsp;

• Strong project management skills, with the ability to juggle multiple campaigns and deadlines&nbsp;

• An excellent eye for detail and the ability to give clear, constructive feedback to non-designers&nbsp;

Nice to have:&nbsp;

• Motion design and animation skills in tools such as After Effects or Jitter&nbsp;

• Short-form video editing in tools such as Premiere Pro, CapCut, or Descript&nbsp;

• Experience designing for events, print, and experiential activations&nbsp;

• Ability to read campaign data and apply it to creative decisions&nbsp;

• Experience building or editing pages in Webflow, HubSpot, or WordPress&nbsp;

• Experience designing for technical audiences such as IT professionals&nbsp;

At Exclaimer, we’re proud to offer a benefits package that reflects our commitment to supporting you professionally, personally, and wherever life takes you.&nbsp;

Alongside competitive pay, you’ll have access to generous paid time off, flexible working options including our XFlex programme and a “work from anywhere” allowance - plus enhanced leave for all new parents, regardless of gender, family structure, or path to parenthood.&nbsp;Our wellbeing offering includes comprehensive healthcare coverage, fully funded insurance and income protection, access to 24/7 virtual care, and mental health, legal and financial support through employee assistance programmes. We help you plan for the future with contributory retirement plans and savings support, and back your day-to-day wellbeing with perks like subscriptions to Calm and Blinkist, fitness and lifestyle credits, global travel assistance and a wide range of discounts. Wherever you're based, you'll find that Exclaimer’s benefits are designed to help you thrive: at work and beyond.

&nbsp;

At Exclaimer, inclusion is more than a policy - it’s part of who we are.

We’re proud to be an equal opportunity employer and welcome applications from people of all backgrounds, experiences, and identities. We consider all candidates fairly and without discrimination irrespective of ethnicity, race, religion, nationality, age, gender, marital status, disability, neurodivergence, caring responsibilities, sexual orientation, or gender identity. We’re building a culture where everyone feels they belong and can thrive, and we’d love for you to be part of it.&nbsp; If you require any reasonable adjustments or support through the application or hiring process, please email the team in confidence via Work@Exclaimer.com to let us know.

&nbsp;

Autism Assessor - ADOS - CYP/Early Years - Hybrid (London)

POSITION: Permanent, Full Time

HOURS: Full time and part time opportunities available. 15 hours per week up to 37.5 hours per week.

LOCATION: Hybrid: In person (London) and remote delivery&nbsp;

REMUNERATION:&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Salary Band - £60,000 to £62,000 FTE. If you're interested in an associate role, rates will be discussed with you.

• Extensive benefits package including Health Cash Plan worth over £1000&nbsp;&nbsp;

&nbsp;

United by our vision. Leading with empathy. Pioneers in curiosity.

Healios exists to bring exceptional healthcare to anyone, anytime, anywhere.&nbsp; By digitising entire clinical pathways, we enable children, adults and their family members to receive and seamlessly transition between clinical services from the comfort of their home.&nbsp;

Innovation is at the heart of what we do as we strive to be the leading provider of neurodevelopmental and associated mental health services.&nbsp; You can find out more about us by clicking here!

Healios is all about helping families feel better and that includes our own families too, which is why we embrace diversity in all its forms and offer unparalleled flexibility for our employees. For more information on what it’s like to be a Healios employee, and our hiring processes, take a look at our Notion page.

&nbsp;

“Great minds don’t think alike”&nbsp;

From our talented tech teams to our standout clinical expertise, we’re bringing great minds together to build more accessible services.&nbsp;&nbsp;

As a Specialist Neurodevelopment Practitioner, you will play a pivotal role in our Neurodevelopment team providing high quality diagnostic assessments for our younger clients (ages 3 years +) as well as in some areas, offering post-diagnostic support to help children, adults and their families understand their diagnosis. This will require both in person and remote delivery and you’ll be able to work with other age ranges (subject to appropriate experience and training).

&nbsp;

What you need to have

• Clinical qualification in:

• Occupational Therapy

• Psychology (Clinical, Counselling or Forensic) or

• Mental Health/ Learning Disability Nursing&nbsp;

• Speech &amp; language therapy&nbsp;

• Paediatrician or

• Social Work

• Clinical registration with HCPC, SWE or NMC

• Previous experience in comprehensive assessment of autism in younger age children (age 3+) with varying and complex needs&nbsp;

• Preference for ADOS and ADI-R (or equivalent) trained and experienced but will consider ADOS training/experience only

• Minimum of 1 years experience of conducting and leading on diagnostic assessments and interventions of children and young people, including younger age groups (3+ years).

• Flexibility to support our mission of bringing healthcare to anyone, anytime, anywhere

• A commitment to ethical practice and adherence to the highest standards of safeguarding of adults/children

&nbsp;

What’s in it for you&nbsp;

• Generous leave entitlement&nbsp;

• 33 days holiday (including Bank Holidays)

• Plus paid Christmas closure (between Christmas and New Year)

• Plus Birthday Leave - paid day off on your birthday

• Plus "Life Leave" - 2 days of extra leave to take when things you can't plan for happen

• Enhanced family friendly policies including a phased return to work and receive full pay

• Paid company sick pay scheme

• Contributory Pension Scheme (6% matched)

• Employee Discount to access a private assessment (for ADHD, Autism or a combined assessment) through our Melios service for your child

• Fully personalised flexible benefits package including; Health Cash Plan, Life Assurance, EAP Service, Will Writing, Critical Illness Cover, employee discount and savings portal, Cycle to Work Scheme, Tech Scheme and Wine Club!

• Access to NHS and Perks at Work discounts, including the Blue Light Card

• Work from anywhere policy&nbsp;

• Free access to co-working spaces&nbsp;

• Company laptop, monitor and keyboard, plus an allowance to purchase additional equipment

• CPD/Growth day per year, plus personal development allowance to invest in your growth&nbsp;

• Clinical Professional Registration Fee - Paid

• Bespoke Healios Training and on demand learning including schedule of monthly CPD for clinicians

&nbsp;

ACCOMMODATIONS

We’re glad to accommodate candidates who need adjustments throughout the hiring process and we're always learning about different accessibility needs to ensure our hiring process is accessible for all candidates. We encourage you to be open about the adjustments you need so we can adapt our interview process. You can read more about Healios being an Inclusive Employer on our Notion page

We are a Disability Confident Employer and operate a Guaranteed Interview Scheme (GIS). This means we are committed to interviewing all disabled applicants who meet the minimum criteria for this role. If you wish to be considered under this scheme, please indicate this when asked about disability on the application form.

&nbsp;
DIVERSITY AND INCLUSION

“Do the right thing” is one of our core Healios values. And building a diverse and inclusive workplace where everyone feels supported is absolutely the right thing to do. Whether we’re developing a new service line or enhancing one of our products, we need people with different skills, backgrounds, identities and perspectives to ensure our innovations will work for the children and young people we are here to serve. By embracing diversity, we can deliver better care experiences and outcomes, while tackling the inequalities in healthcare provision that exist today.

&nbsp;

SAFER RECRUITMENT &amp; PRE- EMPLOYMENT CHECKS&nbsp;

Healios ensures that supporting people to be safe is at the heart of our work and a key priority across all areas of the organisation, We will do our absolute best to keep the people that we support, safe from harm. This starts with our recruitment processes.

As part of our pre-employment checks, all employees of Healios will be asked to have a Disclosure and Barring Service (DBS)&nbsp;check. Dependent&nbsp;on your role within the business, this will either be an Enhanced or Basic.&nbsp;A&nbsp;Protecting Vulnerable Groups (PVG)&nbsp;check&nbsp;will be required. You will also be asked to provide two professional&nbsp;references&nbsp;as a minimum.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Join Our Team at Hydromarque!

Calling curious graduates. Are you…

- the person who wants to understand how something works, not just accept that it does?
- good with numbers, words and questions — particularly the useful sort?
- looking for a first proper career opportunity where you can learn from experienced people and become genuinely valuable?

And are you more than ready…

- to work on real engineering problems that are rarely the same twice?
- to join a friendly small business where people know your name, notice your progress and support you to do well?
- for structured training, increasing responsibility and a career built around practical problem-solving?

You do not need to arrive knowing everything about pumps; all we ask is that you’re keen and willing to learn.

Hydromarque supplies specialist pumping solutions for the water and wastewater industries and holds the UK licence for selected product lines that no other UK supplier can offer. The business is looking for someone with the aptitude and attitude to learn how to turn a customer’s problem into the right technical solution.

The role

This is a development role where you’ll learn the applications-engineering process from experienced colleagues, working with the Hydromarque team in Peterborough. 

For roughly your first three months, the focus will be induction, observation and learning rather than transactional customer work. At around six months, you should be starting to handle straightforward enquiries with support. Becoming fully confident takes time — typically two to three years — because this is a genuine technical career, not a six-week crash course and a new email signature.

The role is primarily office-based. Once you have suitable training and confidence, there may also be opportunities to accompany colleagues on customer site visits.

Your development will include learning how to:

- understand what a customer is really trying to achieve;
- ask clear questions and gather the technical detail needed to assess an application;
- select suitable pumps, systems and associated equipment;

- prepare quotations, tenders and professional customer emails;
- use Hydromarque’s product information and internal systems accurately;
- support technical enquiries by phone and email; and
- take increasing ownership of applications and customer relationships as your knowledge grows.

About you

How many of this list can you tick off? 

- A degree or graduate-level capability, with a solid foundation in Maths and English;
- A practical, analytical approach to problem-solving;
- An inquisitive mind and the confidence to ask questions when you do not yet know the answer;
- Clear spoken communication and professional written English;
- Good Excel skills and general computer literacy;
- Mechanical aptitude or a genuine interest in how equipment and systems work; and
- A proactive, adaptable and team-focused attitude.

An engineering, mechanical, mathematics, physics or related background may be helpful, as would any understanding of hydraulics, but Hydromarque is more interested in how you think and learn than in finding somebody with a perfectly labelled degree certificate.

As a person, you’ll be approachable, willing to help and comfortable becoming part of a close-knit team. You’ll care about getting the details right for customers and be motivated by making a useful contribution to specific industries such as water and food and beverages as well as general industry.

What it’s like to work here

Hydromarque is a small, agile business where the Directors sit with the team, hierarchy is kept to a minimum and everyone gets involved. People support one another, celebrate together and understand that work is important without pretending it is the only important thing in life.

You’ll have the freedom to contribute ideas and, as your capability develops, real autonomy in your role. Hydromarque is also part of the WTR Group, so you gain the close support of a small business alongside the stability, supplier network and longer-term possibilities of a larger international group.

What on offer

- A salary that reflects your starting point;
- 25 days’ annual leave plus Bank Holidays;
- Employer pension contribution of 5% when you contribute 5%;
- Death in Service Benefit (3x salary)
- Relocation assistance may be available for the right candidate;
- A Company-performance bonus scheme;
- Access to the WTR Group employee share scheme;
- Patient, hands-on training and mentoring from experienced colleagues; and
- A structured opportunity to grow into an Applications Engineer and, in time, take on senior applications responsibility.

Interested

If you are looking for your first serious step into engineering — with proper training, unusual problems to solve and people who will have your back while you learn — please apply now. 
Careers@hydromarque.com

Join Our Team at Hydromarque!

Calling experienced pump and hydraulics people. Are you…

- ready to swap layers of sign-off for the freedom to think, question and act?
- wishing you had the opportunity to deal with technical enquiries in more depth than ‘send a price and hope for the best’?
- keen to be known for what you contribute, rather than as employee number 4,783?

And would you like to…

- solve unusual water and wastewater problems using products that no other UK supplier can offer?
- own an enquiry from the first conversation through to a well-considered technical solution?
- join a small, agile business with real autonomy and the backing and network of a larger international group?

Yes, that is quite a specific list. Hydromarque is quite a specific business.

Hydromarque holds the UK licence for selected specialist pump product lines. That means the team can offer solutions customers simply cannot source elsewhere in the UK — and it needs an experienced applications engineer who enjoys working out what will genuinely fit the problem.

The role

This is a technically led, customer-facing role at the heart of Hydromarque. You’ll talk to customers, draw out the detail behind their enquiry, select and develop the right solution, and turn it into clear quotations, tenders and proposals.

You’ll be responsible for:

- Handling technical enquiries by phone and email and asking the questions that uncover the real requirement;
- Having an in-depth understanding of hydraulic systems analyses
- Fostering customer relations by instilling trust through sound engineering advice and customer centric activities
- Reviewing applications and selecting suitable pumps, systems and associated equipment;
- Preparing accurate quotations, tenders and technical proposals;
- Guiding customers through their options and adding value beyond simply selling a product;
- Taking increasing ownership of applications, projects and the Hydromarque customer experience;
- Working closely with colleagues, suppliers and the wider WTR Group; and
- Contributing ideas that improve processes, service and the way the business works.

The role is primarily office-based in Peterborough. Site visits may be an option once you are fully product trained.

Even with strong sector experience, you won’t be expected to know Hydromarque’s specialist product range on day one. You’ll spend time learning alongside the team; realistically, that means a proper period of shadowing and product immersion rather than being handed a catalogue and wished good luck.

About you

How many of this list can you tick off?

- Substantial experience in hydraulics or a closely related environment;
- A sound understanding of applications, systems and how to translate a customer problem into a practical solution;
- A naturally analytical and inquisitive mind — you are comfortable unpacking complexity and are not easily bowled over by the numbers;
- Clear, professional communication, both written and spoken;
- The confidence to engage with customers, ask good questions and work comfortably with people in different roles and environments;
- Good Excel and general computer skills; and
- A proactive, adaptable approach and a genuine desire to add value.

Experience with self-priming pumps, rotating equipment, compressors, water authorities, wastewater, process engineering or technical solution selling could all be useful. Direct pump-sector knowledge is the ideal; an adjacent hydraulics background with strong transferable expertise may also make for a very interesting conversation.

What it’s like to work here

Hydromarque is a small team where Directors sit alongside everyone else, people help one another and there is no unnecessary hierarchy. The team works seriously at getting things right for customers, but does not believe that serious work requires a permanently serious face.

There are team lunches, cook-offs, celebrations and people who understand that you have a life outside work. You’ll be trusted to own your role, encouraged to improve how things are done and able to see the effect of your work. At the same time, Hydromarque is part of the WTR Group, giving the business the stability, supplier relationships and wider network of a much larger organisation while retaining day-to-day autonomy.

What on offer

- A salary that reflects your experience;
- 25 days’ annual leave plus Bank Holidays;
- Employer pension contribution of 5%;
- Death in Service benefit (3x salary);
- Relocation assistance may be available for the right candidate;
- A Company-performance bonus scheme;
- Access to the WTR Group employee share scheme;
- In-depth product training and mentoring; and
- A longer-term route towards senior applications responsibility and succession to a highly experienced member of the team.

Interested

If you want technical depth, visible impact and room to use your judgement in a business where your contribution will be noticed, please apply now.

Careers@hydromarque.com

