## **About Mayday**

We’re an accounting-tech startup building the AI and automation to save finance teams from the pain of manual work. We’re hyper-ambitious with a huge long-term vision. We will mend month end and enable real-time accounting. We have team members in the UK, Australia, New Zealand and South Africa. Australia is our biggest market.

We’re founded by two experienced entrepreneurs: [David Tuck](https://www.linkedin.com/in/tuckdavid/), an accountant then CFO by training who founded Chaser; and [James Scott-Griffin](https://www.linkedin.com/in/jsgriffin/), a software engineer who was CTO at Idio (now Optimizely) and Rungway.

We’ve had a brilliant first three years. We’ve built an incredible initial team. We have [amazing reviews](https://apps.xero.com/uk/app/mayday/reviews) from our customers. We won Xero’s People’s Choice Award in 2025 and 2026, and Practice App of the Year in 2026. We’re backed by elite investors. We recently closed [our Seed round to accelerate](https://www.getmayday.com/blog/mayday-raises-ps3m-au-6m-seed-round) and grow the team to 24.

David has spoken extensively about our journey on his build-in-public blog, [Starting Up Again](https://startingupagain.substack.com/). Our values (with the link to the relevant post explaining each) are:

- [Delight](https://startingupagain.substack.com/p/89-social-architecture-our-values)
- [Ownership](https://startingupagain.substack.com/p/90-social-architecture-our-values)
- [Curiosity](https://startingupagain.substack.com/p/91-social-architecture-our-values)
- [Boldness](https://startingupagain.substack.com/p/92-social-architecture-our-values)
- [Balance](https://startingupagain.substack.com/p/93-social-architecture-our-values)

## **The Role**

We’ve experienced rapid recent growth and are excited to create this Commercial Associate role. You will work alongside and report directly to David, our Co-Founder & CEO. This role is as broad as they come. It will encompass sales, account management, customer success, support, operations, partnerships, and some elements of product and marketing. 

‍

Specifically:

- Delivering demos and sales meetings (predominantly via video call) to prospects (both in-house finance teams and accounting firms) and successfully converting them to paying customers;
- Delivering account management, customer success and customer support to trialists and customers;
- Taking ownership of operational projects as and when they arise. Examples might include: intellectual property protection, selecting and implementing an HR system and putting in place a spend management system;
- Assisting with the development of partnership relationships, both with accounting softwares that we integrate with, and complementary solutions that serve the same target customer base;
- We are rapidly developing our product offering. Your insights about what our customers need will be instrumental to our product roadmap decisions.

‍

There will be a huge breadth of experience, exposure and responsibility. This will be an incredible career-shaping role for the right person. There is so much opportunity for where you take it as we grow.

‍

## **About You**

- First-hand experience of the problems we solve is essential. You will have worked (likely qualified) as an accountant / finance person. You will be fluent in debits and credits. You will be enthusiastic about accounting as a discipline;
- Hyper-organised. There will be so many moving parts to juggle in this role;
- Excitement about sales. You don’t need to be any kind of sales pro, or even have done a sales role before. But the prospect of doing it needs to excite you, not elicit dread;
- A great relationship builder;
- Passionate about great product. You don’t need to be dreaming of a future in product management. But you are someone who is excited and curious about the possibilities of software products;
- An insatiable proactive desire to learn and be challenged.

‍

## **The Details**

- Salary will depend on experience. Given the accounting experience required for this role, we don’t anticipate paying less than £40k per annum;
- Share options from day 1;
- 25 days’ paid holiday, plus public holidays;
- Personal learning and development budget;
- 1 day a week in person in Central London (likely more during onboarding). We will provide co-working membership for the remaining days if needed.

‍

## **Next steps**

Please get in touch at [careers@getmayday.com](mailto:careers@getmayday.com). If you have an up to date CV, then great. But please don’t go to loads of effort to produce one if you don’t. A link to your LinkedIn profile will be fine.

