As part of a dynamic team at ESA/ECSAT, you will have the following responsibilities:
• Support the development of innovative telecommunications satellite technologies and products;
• Contribute to technology and product development activities across a broad range of satellite communication applications;
• Participate in the definition, maintenance, and control of technical requirements, specifications, and associated documentation;
• Support the evaluation, negotiation, monitoring, and management of development contracts and related activities;
• Prepare status reports, work plans, technical documentation, and review materials for key stakeholders;
• Collaborate with technical experts and project teams across multiple telecommunications initiatives.
• Monitor industry trends, emerging technologies, and market developments within the satellite communications sector;
• Support ARTES programme activities, including market intelligence, socioeconomic analysis, risk identification, and project lifecycle management;

• Master's degree (or equivalent) in Engineering, Physics, Telecommunications, Aerospace Engineering, or a related discipline;
• Minimum of 4 years' experience in the development, design, manufacturing, or testing of aerospace and/or telecommunications satellite equipment and subsystems;
• Strong understanding of low-level technical solution definition and implementation within complex engineering environments;
• Proven expertise in one or more of the following areas:• Satellite payload hardware and onboard processing system architectures;
• End-to-end satellite communications systems engineering;

• Experience or knowledge of spacecraft platform subsystems would be considered an advantage, including:• Propulsion systems
• Electrical power systems
• AOCS (Attitude and Orbit Control Systems)
• TT&C systems
• Onboard data processing units

• Ability to work effectively both independently and within multicultural, international teams;
• Strong communication, stakeholder management, and problem-solving skills;
• Eligibility to obtain ESA/EU Security Clearance;
• Fluent English, both written and spoken.

We currently have two opportunities available, one based in Harwell, UK and one in Noordwijk, Netherlands.
